Don't sigh.  Although the discussion originally centered on the
nymph/seduction bit, I do not recall arguing that sex appeal and
charisma should be identified.  My feeling about women having
greater overall charisma was based on my observation that they
tend to be less physically aggressive and also less threatening.
Of course, this would only affect charisma as it pertains to a
very narrow range of "charismatic" scenarios.

I do recall thinking it would be interesting if male humans
tended not to land the first blow on females, but I don't think
I tied this directly in with the overall question of charisma.
Men just tend to underestimate women, and to focus on the re-
gion between the neck and stomach.  I argued that women monsters
should have a decided advantage in landing the first blow.  Maybe
in NetHack terms this would have to translate into stealth - which
women would excel at due to their lesser size coupled with equal
physical agility.

Although I didn't make a point of it, I really think that the most
important tradeoff for being female should be a simple strength/
food requirement one.  Strength is one of the single greatest as-
sets one can have in NetHack, though, so I spent a lot of time
grasping at various ways to make up for the difference (see above
on the "first blow" bit).

In the future I will try to refer to male-female distinctions as
based on "gender" rather than "sex."  This way it will become more
clear what I have on my mind.  Since I had a lot to say about sex
as well, I'm not shocked that it seemed I was talking about sex-
appeal throughout.

-Richard


